---
layout: base
title: Developers
description: Developer portal for NobodyWho - install the on-device inference SDK for any platform, browse the model catalog, and access the public data API and OpenAPI spec.
tags: pageHiddenInMenu
permalink: "/developers/"
---

<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32 lg:px-8">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-5xl dark:text-white">Developers</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-pretty text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Everything you need to build with NobodyWho, the inference engine that runs LLMs fully
            on-device. No servers, no API keys, no hidden fees &mdash; inference happens on the user's
            hardware. This portal covers install commands for every platform, quickstarts, the model
            catalog, and a public data API for tools and agents.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a href="https://docs.nobodywho.ooo/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-1.5 rounded-full bg-neutral-950 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-neutral-700 dark:bg-white dark:text-black dark:hover:bg-neutral-200">Documentation</a>
            <a href="{{ site.github_url }}" class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-1.5 rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-900 ring-1 ring-neutral-300 hover:bg-neutral-50 dark:text-white dark:ring-white/15 dark:hover:bg-white/5">{% svg "github", "size-4" %} GitHub</a>
            <a href="/openapi.json" class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-1.5 rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-900 ring-1 ring-neutral-300 hover:bg-neutral-50 dark:text-white dark:ring-white/15 dark:hover:bg-white/5">OpenAPI spec</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Install by platform -->
    <section class="mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">Install the SDK</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
            NobodyWho ships as a native SDK for each platform. Pick yours and add it to your project.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
            {% for platform in platforms %}
            <div class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl p-6 ring-1 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-white/10">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">{{ platform.name }}</h3>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">{{ platform.language }}</p>
                {% if platform.install %}
                <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-neutral-950 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-neutral-100 dark:bg-black"><code>{{ platform.install }}</code></pre>
                {% else %}
                <p class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-neutral-300">Add via {{ platform.packageManager }}.</p>
                {% endif %}
                <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm">
                    <a href="{{ platform.docsUrl }}" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Docs</a>
                    {% if platform.starterUrl %}<a href="{{ platform.starterUrl }}" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Starter project</a>{% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Quickstart -->
    <section class="mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">Quickstart</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Load a GGUF model and start chatting &mdash; here in Python. See the
            <a href="https://docs.nobodywho.ooo/" class="text-primary hover:underline">docs</a> for every language.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
            {% include "partials/index/snippets/_python.njk" %}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Need a model? Browse our <a href="/models/" class="text-primary hover:underline">recommended selection</a>
            or query it programmatically below. These are just recommendations &mdash; NobodyWho runs
            <strong>any</strong> compatible model: text generation in GGUF, and speech-to-text, text-to-speech
            and voice activity detection in ONNX, loaded from Hugging Face or any URL.
        </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Data API -->
    <section class="mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">Data API</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
            A public, read-only JSON API describing the model catalog, supported platforms and the blog.
            No authentication, CORS enabled, safe for tools and agents. Described by an
            <a href="/openapi.json" class="text-primary hover:underline">OpenAPI&nbsp;3.1 spec</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-white/10">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                <thead class="bg-neutral-50 text-neutral-500 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-neutral-400">
                    <tr>
                        <th class="px-6 py-3 font-medium">Endpoint</th>
                        <th class="px-6 py-3 font-medium">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-neutral-200 dark:divide-white/10">
                    <tr>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3"><a href="/api/models.json" class="font-mono text-primary hover:underline">GET /api/models.json</a></td>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">Recommended on-device model selection (NobodyWho runs any GGUF/ONNX model)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3"><a href="/api/platforms.json" class="font-mono text-primary hover:underline">GET /api/platforms.json</a></td>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">Supported SDK platforms &amp; install commands</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3"><a href="/api/posts.json" class="font-mono text-primary hover:underline">GET /api/posts.json</a></td>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">Blog posts and tutorials</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3"><a href="/api/index.json" class="font-mono text-primary hover:underline">GET /api/index.json</a></td>
                        <td class="px-6 py-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">API discovery document</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Live model search. The toolname/tooldescription attributes expose this
             form to browser-resident AI agents via WebMCP; it also works as a normal
             client-side filter over /api/models.json. -->
        <div class="mt-10" x-data="modelSearch()">
            <form
                toolname="search_models"
                tooldescription="Search NobodyWho's recommended on-device model catalog by name, lab, capability or target device."
                @submit.prevent="search()"
                class="flex max-w-xl gap-3">
                <label for="model-query" class="sr-only">Search the model catalog</label>
                <input
                    id="model-query"
                    name="query"
                    type="search"
                    x-model="query"
                    @input.debounce.200ms="search()"
                    placeholder="Search models: gemma, smartphone, speech to text…"
                    class="w-full rounded-lg border border-neutral-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-neutral-900 placeholder:text-neutral-400 focus:border-primary focus:outline-none dark:border-white/15 dark:bg-neutral-900 dark:text-white"/>
                <button type="submit" class="rounded-lg bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-primary-700 dark:bg-primary-600 dark:hover:bg-primary-500">Search</button>
            </form>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400" x-show="ready" x-text="results.length + ' model(s) match'"></p>
            <ul class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2" x-show="ready">
                <template x-for="m in results.slice(0, 12)" :key="m.family + m.variant">
                    <li class="rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm ring-1 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-white/10">
                        <span class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white" x-text="m.family + ' ' + m.variant"></span>
                        <span class="text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400" x-text="' · ' + m.pipeline + ' · ' + m.idealDeviceDeployment"></span>
                    </li>
                </template>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- For AI agents -->
    <section class="mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">For AI agents</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
            NobodyWho is built to be machine-readable. Agents can discover and integrate with this site through:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 max-w-2xl space-y-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
            <li><a href="/llms.txt" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">/llms.txt</a> &mdash; a concise, LLM-friendly map of the site.</li>
            <li><a href="/openapi.json" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">/openapi.json</a> &mdash; OpenAPI 3.1 description of the data API.</li>
            <li><a href="/api/index.json" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">/api/index.json</a> &mdash; the data API discovery document.</li>
            <li><strong>WebMCP</strong> &mdash; browser-resident agents can call in-page tools
                (<code class="text-sm">search_models</code>, <code class="text-sm">get_install_command</code>,
                <code class="text-sm">list_platforms</code>, <code class="text-sm">list_blog_posts</code>)
                registered via <code class="text-sm">document.modelContext</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

<script>
    function modelSearch() {
        return {
            query: "",
            results: [],
            all: [],
            ready: false,
            async init() {
                try {
                    const res = await fetch("/api/models.json", { headers: { Accept: "application/json" } });
                    const json = await res.json();
                    this.all = json.data || [];
                    this.results = this.all;
                    this.ready = true;
                } catch (e) {
                    this.ready = false;
                }
            },
            search() {
                const q = this.query.toLowerCase().trim();
                if (!q) { this.results = this.all; return; }
                this.results = this.all.filter((m) =>
                    [m.lab, m.family, m.variant, m.pipeline, m.pipelineLabel, m.idealDeviceDeployment]
                        .join(" ").toLowerCase().includes(q)
                );
            },
        };
    }
</script>
